file src/gui/mod.rs
symbol Action
lines 0 25
hash c5362cc361e22e46
note What a click can ask for. Navigation, selection, the per-step view toggles, opening a group, the two deletions, tab switches and the three commands the top bar offers. Adding a gesture means adding a variant here and an arm in apply, not threading a callback through the panels. The fields are positional: a (path, step) pair indexes map.paths and that path's anchors; GoTo, Jump and PeekAt take a file index and 0-based line (and column), Jump and PeekAt meaning the definition of the identifier there; SelectLine's bool extends the listing selection; SelectStep's bool says the click was inside the document; OpenPath selects the path unless it is the one being read and shows it in the given tab; CollapseAll's bool hides every step's code, false showing all and unfolding all; FoldAll's bool folds every step with children, false unfolding all; OpenGroup's bool opens or closes the group; Context's i8 is -1 for more lines above, 1 for more below and 0 for back to the slice.

step jdewtv
order 30
parent d5you8
author ai
file src/gui/document.rs
symbol doc_steps
lines 0 283
hash 763c25fba0b81912
note The steps of one path in tree order, each a header with the hierarchical number and the fold, hide-code, whole-symbol, link and delete controls, then the note and the anchored lines. The same function draws a linked path inline: occ tells its element ids apart, the numbers carry the linking step's number as a prefix, and chain stops a path from opening inside itself. occ is None for the path being read; each inline expansion takes a fresh number from next_occ, so its ids differ from the path's own and from another expansion of the same path. Clicking a header of the path being read selects the step where it is, while a step of an inline linked path opens that path. The toggle buttons keep one width whatever their label, and the delete button sits alone at the far right, so no button slides under a pointer that clicks twice.

